    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="usage-leaders">
      <p class="sub">Ranked by % of meta within the selected tier and filters. Click a column header to re-sort.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table id="usage-leaders-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Pokémon</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="usage_share">% of meta</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="win-rate-leaders" hidden>
      <div class="controls">
        <label>Min. recorded matches
          <select id="win-rate-min-record-count-filter">
            <option value="5">5+</option>
            <option value="10">10+</option>
            <option value="20">20+</option>
            <option value="50">50+</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-6xn" id="win-rate-grid"></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table id="win-rate-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Pokémon</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="win_rate">Win rate</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="usage-success" hidden>
      <p class="sub">
        Popular is not the same as successful. Raw usage counts a last-place
        team's roster slot exactly like a winner's; these two views weight it
        by where the team actually finished
        (<code>tournament_team.placement</code>).
        <strong>Top cut</strong> counts only appearances on a team that placed
        1&#8211;8; <strong>placement-weighted</strong> weights every appearance
        by 1/placement, so a win counts far more than a 200th with no cutoff
        cliff. The <strong>Movement</strong> column is how many places a
        Pokémon gains or loses versus its raw usage rank — a positive number is
        a quiet top-cut staple, a negative one is a crowd favourite that
        underperforms.
      </p>
      <div class="controls">
        <label>Ranked by
          <select id="usage-success-metric">
            <option value="placement_weighted">Placement-weighted</option>
            <option value="top_cut">Top cut (1&#8211;8)</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-6xn" id="usage-success-grid"></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table id="usage-success-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Pokémon</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="weighted_usage_share">Weighted share</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="top_cut_usage_share">Top-cut share</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="usage_share">Raw usage</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="rank_movement">Movement</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="subtab-panel" data-subpanel="usage-trends" hidden>
      <p class="sub">Usage by tournament date (<code>tournament_event.event_date</code>), not by extraction snapshot — this shows how usage shifted across events actually played. Change is versus the previous tournament date in the data, not a fixed time window.</p>
      <div class="controls">
        <label>Tournament date
          <select id="usage-trend-date-filter"></select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-6xn" id="usage-trend-grid"></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table id="usage-trend-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Pokémon</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="usage_share">% of meta</th><th class="sortable" data-sort-key="usage_share_delta">Change</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

