  <section class="tab-panel" data-panel="archetypes" hidden>
    <h2>Detected Archetypes</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Experimental, data-derived team identities anchored by three-Pokémon
      cores from real Champions rosters. Qualifying cores appear on at least
      five teams and have above-chance three-way and average pair lift. Cores
      sharing two members consolidate under their strongest neighbour; teams
      receive one primary assignment and may retain one near-tied secondary
      assignment. Neutral core names are deliberate—composition alone does
      not prove an editorial label such as “Rain” or “Balance.”
    </p>
    <div class="grid-6xn" id="detected-archetype-grid"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="tab-panel" data-panel="speed-tiers" hidden>
    <h2>Speed tiers</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Who actually moves first, under the scenario you pick. Everything but
      "Base stat" is <strong>max Speed investment</strong> at Level 50 (252
      EVs, a beneficial nature, a 31 IV) — the documented convention in
      <code>pokemon_champions_profile</code>, since no source publishes real
      per-roster EV spreads. Choose an opposing Speed to see who outruns it.
    </p>
    <div class="controls">
